<p>President Donald Trump delivered his first official State of the Union address of his second term to a joint session of Congress in Washington on February 24. In a record-length speech, he argued the United States has entered a “golden age” and urged Republicans to rally ahead of November’s midterm elections. Multiple outlets described a sharply polarized scene, with loud Republican applause and protests, heckling, and some Democratic boycotts during the address. Trump leaned heavily on domestic themes—especially the economy, tariffs, and immigration enforcement—while also spotlighting foreign-policy priorities, most notably Iran and nuclear weapons. On Iran, he said he preferred diplomacy but insisted he would never allow Tehran to obtain a nuclear weapon. Coverage broadly echoed that message, noting ongoing nuclear talks alongside administration warnings about possible military action if diplomacy fails. In other international remarks, several reports highlighted Trump’s claims about his role in easing tensions between India and Pakistan, while other coverage questioned parts of those assertions and noted analysts disagree on how decisive his role was.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/fY5S52jCVoGe6oPz_KPsLhrHMXk7FJLFAPq_Ze6sp-0nQy_Ay_-6gQS0LyFqmKiNTFjx6FIAFpCahANXSAG14zwb-Ql1iI1D7aIxZENgekFAptMIfYi2Y3OSs4bWASiZNlyEYw9pyr4nyYeKnlAWSrOz4Q9iyD-V2GtiTNj40d2OwDZdT5EdXRAVNgCFq8phSL2BCi0jbnSc5JhUPqMfbbMIdCquf69Uqkq_hkFgyk0AmyYpWDnPMorjxUQpAyhdnMw-E6v7QuTSG28FXw' alt='President Donald Trump delivers the State of the Union address to a joint session of Congress at the US Capitol on February 24, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Tariff strategy: Trump said he would press ahead with a new tariff regime without Congress after the Supreme Court struck down his sweeping emergency tariffs, including citing Section 122 of the Trade Act of 1974 for a 10% global tariff that he said he may raise to 15%.</li><li>Iran talks: Trump said his “preference” was diplomacy but demanded Iran give “those secret words” that it would never have a nuclear weapon. Reports described ongoing negotiations alongside warnings about potential military action if diplomacy fails.</li><li>Ukraine pledge: Trump pledged to keep negotiating to end the war in Ukraine, according to coverage of the address.</li><li>Energy for AI: Trump said agreements would require major technology companies to supply their own electricity for new AI-driven data centers so consumer power bills don’t rise.</li><li>Chamber disruptions: Coverage highlighted visible Democratic protest inside the chamber, including Democratic Representative Al Green being escorted out early in the address after holding up a protest sign.</li></ul><blockquote>My preference is to solve this problem through diplomacy, but one thing is certain: I will never allow the world’s number one sponsor of terror—which they are by far—to have a nuclear weapon - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Democratic lawmakers: Coverage described protests and some boycotts during the speech. One report said Democratic Representative Al Green was escorted out early after holding up a protest sign, while other Democrats remained seated and at times heckled as Republicans repeatedly applauded. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/25/trump-defends-immigration-crackdowns-and-tariffs-in-longest-ever-state-of-the-union-addres'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump called his first year back in office a “turnaround for the ages,” crediting tax cuts, deregulation, tariffs, and immigration enforcement for what he described as a new “golden age”. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633005-trump-state-union-address/'>RT</a>)</li><li>BBC analysis: A BBC analysis said Trump delivered a patriotic rallying cry designed to energize his base and needle opponents with the midterms in view. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2d7x6zrwro'>BBC</a>)</li><li>The Guardian: The Guardian reported Trump offered relatively few new policy pledges and used the speech to attack political opponents, as he faced low approval ratings and criticism over cost-of-living pressures. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/24/trump-state-of-the-union-address'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Iran-focused coverage: Reports said Trump paired talk of diplomacy with “peace through strength” signaling, including claims that Iran is pursuing missiles that could reach the United States and references to last year’s strikes on Iranian nuclear sites, while still insisting he would not allow Tehran to obtain a nuclear weapon. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975653/trump-keeps-the-world-guessing-on-his-iran-options-during-annual-state-of-the-union-speech'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-trump-delivers-state-of-the-union-address/a-76110624'>US: Trump delivers State of the Union address</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-02-24-0800/donald-trump-clashes-democrats-dominate-trumps-state-union'>Clashes with Democrats dominate Trump&#x27;s State of the Union</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/us-politics/article-trump-state-of-the-union-address-declining-support/'>In State of the Union address, Trump touts economic agenda amid declining support</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975653/trump-keeps-the-world-guessing-on-his-iran-options-during-annual-state-of-the-union-speech'>Trump keeps the world guessing on his Iran options during annual State of the Union speech</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/25/trump-to-boast-of-turnaround-for-the-ages-in-state-of-the-union-according-to-speech-snippet-released-by-white-house_6750851_4.html'>&#x27;This is the Golden Age of America,&#x27; Trump declares in State of the Union address</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/n